rrorCode.InvalidParams, `No completion target: ${JSON.stringify(req.params.ref)}`);\n./test/e2e/scenarios/completion.test.ts:163:        ).rejects.toMatchObject({ code: ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams });\n./test/e2e/scenarios/completion.test.ts:320:            s.setRequestHandler('resources/read', () => ({ contents: [] }));\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-stamping.test.ts:5: * - the entryModern cell (2026-07-28 axis): typed tools/list, resources/read\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-stamping.test.ts:10: *   hint (resources/read), a per-operation hint wins over the defaults\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-stamping.test.ts:43: * - a per-operation hint for resources/read AND a per-resource hint on the\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-stamping.test.ts:54:                'resources/read': { ttlMs: 90_000, cacheScope: 'public' }\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-stamping.test.ts:120:    // hint wins over the defaults); resources/read shows the per-resource\n./test/e2e/scenarios/jsonschema.test.ts:49: * captures per-tool and surfaces as `InvalidParams`.\n./test/e2e/scenarios/jsonschema.test.ts:101:                throw new ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, `unknown tool ${req.params.name}`);\n./test/e2e/scenarios/jsonschema.test.ts:133:    expect(err.code).toBe(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams);\n./test/e2e/scenarios/jsonschema.test.ts:155:    expect(err.code).toBe(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams);\n./test/e2e/scenarios/jsonschema.test.ts:219:    expect(err.code).toBe(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams);\n./test/e2e/scenarios/jsonschema.test.ts:252:    expect(err.code).toBe(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams);\n./test/e2e/scenarios/errors.test.ts:136:    expect(rejection.code).toBe(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams);\n./test/e2e/scenarios/sampling.test.ts:342:    expect(r.structuredContent).toMatchObject({ ok: false, code: ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams });\n./test/e2e/scenarios/sampling.test.ts:393:    expect(missing.structuredContent).toMatchObject({ ok: false, code: ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams });\n./test/e2e/scenarios/sampling.test.ts:408:    expect(trailing.structuredContent).toMatchObject({ ok: false, code: ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams });\n./test/e2e/scenarios/protocol.test.ts:406:    // -32602 InvalidParams at the protocol layer (not McpServer's tool-arg validation).\n./test/e2e/scenarios/protocol.test.ts:431:    expect(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams).toBe(-32_602);\n./test/e2e/scenarios/protocol.test.ts:432:    await expect(call).rejects.toMatchObject({ code: ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams });\n./docs/servers/prompts.md:154:`prompts/get` returns the style guide inline as the first message, so the client never makes a second `resources/read` round trip:\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:519:            'A tool whose advertised outputSchema declares a $schema dialect URI the built-in validator does not recognise is refused gracefully on the client: callTool throws InvalidParams with a clear \"unsupported dialect … 2020-12 only\" message instead of having the underlying engine fail opaquely.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:524:            'One bad outputSchema in a tools/list response (a schema the validator engine refuses to compile — e.g. an unresolvable external $ref) does not poison the listing: tools/list resolves with every tool present, callTool on the bad tool throws InvalidParams, and callTool on the other tools succeeds.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:547:            'A tool whose advertised outputSchema declares no $schema is validated by the client with the 2020-12 engine (the default): a 2020-12-only keyword (prefixItems) in the schema is enforced, so structuredContent violating it causes callTool to throw InvalidParams.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:726:        behavior: 'resources/read returns binary contents base64-encoded in blob.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:730:        behavior: 'Variables extracted from a templated resource URI reach the resource function as typed arguments.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:734:        behavior: 'resources/read returns text contents carrying uri, mimeType, and the text.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:739:            'resources/read for an unknown URI returns JSON-RPC error -32602 (Invalid Params) with data.uri echoing the requested URI; clients also recognise -32002 from older peers. Servers do not return an empty contents array for a non-existent resource.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:794:            'The deprecated McpServer.resource() overloads (fixed-URI and ResourceTemplate, with and without the optional metadata arg) register a resource that surfaces in resources/list and reads via resources/read identically to registerResource().',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:900:            'completion/complete with a ref naming an unknown prompt or non-matching resource URI returns JSON-RPC error -32602 (Invalid params).'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:963:                note: 'Protocol wraps schema-parse failures as -32603 (InternalError), not -32602 (InvalidParams) as required by JSON-RPC 2.0.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2504:            'A resource_link returned by a tool call can be followed with resources/read on the linked URI to retrieve the referenced contents.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2505:        note: 'Stateless hosting creates a fresh server per request and has no standalone GET stream, so there is no server→client channel to deliver/observe these. The createMcpHandler entry arms are included: the body is plain client→server request/response (a tools/call, then a resources/read against the same statically-registered factory), so the per-request entry serves it on both eras.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2658:            'Typed tools/list, resources/read and resources/list round trips negotiated on 2026-07-28 over a createMcpHandler endpoint succeed, and the wire results carry resultType \"complete\" plus the required ttlMs/cacheScope fields, with the configured-hint precedence observable on the wire: the per-resource cacheHint wins over the per-operation cacheHints entry (resources/read), a per-operation hint wins over the defaults (tools/list), and a result with no configured author is filled with the ttlMs 0 / cacheScope private defaults (resources/list).',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2666:            'A factory with every cache-hint author configured (per-operation cacheHints and a per-resource cacheHint), served to a plain 2025 client through the legacy stateless slot of a createMcpHandler endpoint, answers tools/list and resources/read with no resultType, ttlMs, cacheScope or cacheHint vocabulary anywhere in the response bytes.',\n./docs/servers/input-required.md:6:An **`input_required`** result is how a `tools/call`, `prompts/get`, or `resources/read` handler asks the connected client for input mid-call: the handler returns the embedded requests, the client answers them and retries the call, and the handler runs again with the responses.\n./docs/clients/subscriptions.md:32:The server narrows the filter to its advertised capabilities — `resourceSubscriptions` survives only when it advertises `resources: { subscribe: true }`, and each list-change field only when the matching `listChanged` capability is set. The four filter fields are `toolsListChanged`, `promptsListChanged`, `resourcesListChanged`, and `resourceSubscriptions` (an array of resource URIs).\n./docs/servers/errors.md:112:            throw new ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, `Note ids are lowercase letters, got \"${noteId}\"`);\n./docs/servers/errors.md:146:Pick by audience. The model drives `tools/call`, so a failure it can recover from — a missing record, a bad argument, a transient upstream fault — belongs in `isError: true` with a message that names the fix. The host application drives `resources/read`, `prompts/get`, and `completion/complete`, so failures there are protocol errors addressed to the caller's code.\n./docs/servers/errors.md:166:The error carries the requested URI in `data` and the code the spec mandates for a `resources/read` miss:\n./docs/servers/errors.md:193:| `InvalidParams` | `-32602` | The params are wrong — also the code for a `resources/read` miss. |\n./docs/servers/errors.md:195:| `ResourceNotFound` | `-32002` | Receive-tolerated only: the SDK answers a `resources/read` miss with `-32602` and never emits `-32002`. Throw `ResourceNotFoundError` instead. |\n./docs/servers/resources.md:32:`resources/list` now advertises `config://app` with that metadata, and `resources/read` on `config://app` runs the callback.\n./docs/servers/resources.md:255:On [2026-07-28](../protocol-versions.md) connections the verb does not exist: clients name resource URIs in their `subscriptions/listen` filter, and the entry filters delivery itself — `serveStdio` routes the instance's own `sendResourceUpdated` call onto matching streams, and `createMcpHandler` delivers what you publish on its notifier ([Notifications](./notifications.md#publish-a-resource-update-through-the-handler)).\n./docs/migration/upgrade-to-v2.md:877:| Invalid params (server response)                 | `McpError` + `ErrorCode.InvalidParams`    | `ProtocolError` + `ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams`                |\n./docs/migration/upgrade-to-v2.md:1011:`resources/read` for an unknown URI now answers `-32602` on every protocol revision\n./docs/migration/upgrade-to-v2.md:1511:- **Unknown / disabled tool calls now reject** with `ProtocolError(-32602 InvalidParams)`\n./docs/migration/upgrade-to-v2.md:1601:  tool, as `ProtocolError(InvalidParams, \"Tool 'X' has an invalid outputSchema: …\")`,\n./docs/migration/upgrade-to-v2.md:1727:shutdown wording; transports-as-bindings reframe; `resources/read` wording (the\n./packages/codemod/src/migrations/v1-to-v2/mappings/specSchemaNames.ts:108:    'ReadResourceRequestParamsSchema',\n./packages/codemod/src/migrations/v1-to-v2/mappings/specSchemaNames.ts:109:    'ReadResourceRequestSchema',\n./packages/codemod/src/migrations/v1-to-v2/mappings/specSchemaNames.ts:110:    'ReadResourceResultSchema',\n./docs/clients/roots.md:7:Pass paths through tool arguments, resource URIs, or host configuration instead. **Roots** are deprecated as of protocol version 2026-07-28 (SEP-2577) and stay functional on 2025-era connections for at least twelve months — see the [deprecated features registry](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft/deprecated).\n./docs/clients/roots.md:82:- Roots are deprecated (SEP-2577): pass paths through tool arguments, resource URIs, or configuration instead.\n./docs/migration/support-2026-07-28.md:417:`inputRequired(...)` from a `tools/call` / `prompts/get` / `resources/read` handler; the\n./docs/migration/support-2026-07-28.md:511:already render — while `prompts/get` / `resources/read` failures surface as JSON-RPC\n./docs/clients/caching.md:24:resources/read requests that reached the server: 1\n./docs/clients/caching.md:39:            'resources/read': { ttlMs: 5_000, cacheScope: 'private' }\n./docs/clients/caching.md:45:`registerResource` also takes a per-resource `cacheHint`; it wins, field by field, over the `resources/read` entry here for that resource's read results. Mark a result `cacheScope: 'public'` only when it is identical for every caller — anything derived from the caller's authorization context stays `'private'`, the default.\n./docs/clients/caching.md:59:`responseCacheStore` swaps the backing store; the default is a fresh `InMemoryResponseCacheStore` per client, holding at most 512 `resources/read` entries.\n./packages/codemod/src/migrations/v1-to-v2/mappings/schemaToMethodMap.ts:8:    ReadResourceRequestSchema: 'resources/read',\n./examples/cli-client/README.md:74:| Resources          | `@todos:todos://board` in a message, `/resources` | `resources/read` → injected as a provenance-labelled context block; `list_changed` keeps the cached list fresh                                                         |\n./examples/cli-client/host/host.ts:235:    /** Resolve a `server:uri` reference (the part after the `@`) to the owning server and the resource URI. */\n./examples/cli-client/host/content.ts:1:import type { CallToolResult, ContentBlock, ReadResourceResult } from '@modelcontextprotocol/client';\n./examples/cli-client/host/content.ts:79:export function resourceToContextText(serverName: string, uri: string, result: ReadResourceResult): string {\n./examples/caching/server.ts:5: * result types (the list operations and `resources/read`). The values are\n./examples/caching/server.ts:43:    // own resources/read result.\n./examples/caching/server.ts:61:    // Exposes the server-side `resources/read` invocation count so the client\n./examples/caching/server.ts:63:    server.registerTool('read-count', { description: 'Number of resources/read calls that reached this server' }, async () => ({\n./examples/repl/server.ts:27:import type { CallToolResult, PrimitiveSchemaDefinition, ReadResourceResult, ResourceLink } from '@modelcontextprotocol/server';\n./examples/repl/server.ts:224:        async (uri): Promise<ReadResourceResult> => ({\n./examples/repl/server.ts:233:        async (uri, vars): Promise<ReadResourceResult> => ({ contents: [{ uri: uri.href, text: `Hello, ${vars.name}!` }] })\n./examples/repl/server.ts:244:        async (uri, vars): Promise<ReadResourceResult> => {\n./examples/repl/client.ts:20:    ReadResourceRequest,\n./examples/repl/client.ts:250:                throw new ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, `Unsupported elicitation mode: ${request.params.mode}`);\n./examples/repl/client.ts:791:        const request: ReadResourceRequest = {\n./examples/repl/client.ts:792:            method: 'resources/read',\n./examples/guides/advanced/custom-methods.examples.ts:64:    throw new Error('custom-methods.md tip claim failed: invalid params were accepted');\n./packages/codemod/test/integration.test.ts:51:            `const code = ErrorCode.InvalidParams;`,\n./packages/codemod/test/integration.test.ts:74:        expect(output).toContain('ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams');\n./examples/guides/servers/input-required.examples.ts:238:    if (code !== ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams) throw error;\n./examples/guides/clients/caching.examples.ts:39:                'resources/read': { ttlMs: 5_000, cacheScope: 'private' }\n./examples/guides/clients/caching.examples.ts:93:console.log('resources/read requests that reached the server:', reached.get('resources/read'));\n./examples/guides/clients/caching.examples.ts:98:if (reached.get('tools/list') !== 2 || reached.get('resources/read') !== 1) {\n./examples/guides/clients/caching.examples.ts:99:    throw new Error(`caching.md claim failed: tools/list=${reached.get('tools/list')}, resources/read=${reached.get('resources/read')}`);\n./examples/guides/servers/errors.examples.ts:66:            throw new ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, `Note ids are lowercase letters, got \"${noteId}\"`);\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:39:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Results of the cacheable 2026-07-28 operations (`tools/list`, `prompts/list`, `resources/list`, `resources/templates/list`, `resources/read`, `server/discover`) now always carry the revision's required `ttlMs`/`cacheScope` fields when served on that revision, defaulting to `ttlMs: 0` / `cacheScope: 'private'`. Servers can configure the emitted values with the new `ServerOptions.cacheHints` option (per operation) and the new `cacheHint` member of the `registerResource` config (per resource); resolution is per field, most specific author first: cache fields returned by a handler win over the per-resource hint, which wins over the per-operation hint, and configured hints are validated at construction/registration time (`RangeError` on invalid values). Responses on 2025-era connections are unchanged and never carry these fields. Note for untyped callers: `registerResource` now interprets a `cacheHint` key in its config object — it is validated and kept out of the resource's list metadata, where it was previously passed through as ordinary metadata.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:52:- [#2381](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2381) [`f0bf785`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/f0bf785239af67f0cfce24575fec9c1193deaff1) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Serve `input_required` handlers on 2025-era connections: the legacy shim (on by default) converts each embedded request of an `input_required` return into a real server→client request (`elicitation/create`, `sampling/createMessage`, `roots/list`) over the live session — stamped with the originating request's id for stream association — and re-enters the handler with the collected `inputResponses` until a final result. Handlers are written once in the 2026 `inputRequired(...)` style and serve both eras; the previous loud `-32603` failure remains available via `ServerOptions.inputRequired.legacyShim: false`. Knobs: `inputRequired.maxRounds` (default 8) and `inputRequired.roundTimeoutMs` (default 600 000 ms per leg; legs carry a progressToken so a client reporting progress mid-leg resets the leg timeout). Semantics mirror the modern client driver exactly: per-round replaced `inputResponses`, byte-exact `requestState` echo with the verify hook running every round, paced requestState-only rounds, and elicitation accepted content passed through UNVALIDATED (the handler validates via the schema-aware `acceptedContent` overload, exactly as on the 2026 era). URL-mode legs synthesize the `elicitationId` the 2025-11-25 wire requires. Failures surface per family (`tools/call` → `isError` tool result; `prompts/get` / `resources/read` → JSON-RPC error); stateless legacy HTTP degrades to a clean capability refusal; the shim emits no progress of its own (the originating progressToken is the handler's single must-increase stream — the shim never adds a second author to it).\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:62:  client, an `input_required` answer to `tools/call`, `prompts/get`, or `resources/read` on a 2026-07-28 connection is now fulfilled automatically by default: the embedded requests are dispatched to the client's already-registered elicitation/sampling/roots handlers, and the\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:68:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Add the server side of multi round-trip requests (protocol revision 2026-07-28, SEP-2322). Handlers for `tools/call`, `prompts/get`, and `resources/read` can return the value built by `inputRequired()` (exported from the server package together with `acceptedContent()`)\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:74:  wire behavior is unchanged. An optional `ServerOptions.requestState.verify` hook lets a server integrity-check the echoed `requestState` before the handler runs — a throw answers the wire-level `-32602` Invalid Params error with `data.reason: 'invalid_request_state'`; the SDK provides no default verification.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:76:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - `resources/read` for an unknown URI now answers with JSON-RPC error code `-32602`\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:77:  (Invalid Params) on every protocol revision, with `error.data.uri` echoing the\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:99:    The Streamable HTTP transport now emits the `Mcp-Name` standard header on every modern-enveloped request (`params.name` for `tools/call`/`prompts/get`, `params.uri` for `resources/read`), sentinel-encoded.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:103:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - SEP-2243 standard-header server-side validation (protocol revision 2026-07-28). On the modern (2026-07-28) serving path, `createMcpHandler` now enforces the required `Mcp-Method` and `Mcp-Name` standard request headers in addition to the existing `MCP-Protocol-Version` and `Mcp-Method` cross-checks: a modern request without an `Mcp-Method` header, a `tools/call` / `prompts/get` / `resources/read` request without an `Mcp-Name` header, an `Mcp-Name` header carrying an invalid `=?base64?…?=` sentinel, and an `Mcp-Name` header whose (decoded) value disagrees with the body's `params.name` / `params.uri` are all rejected with `400 Bad Request` and JSON-RPC `-32020` (`HeaderMismatch`). The 2025-era serving paths are unchanged.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:134:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Pin the modern (2026-07-28) HTTP serving path's rejection codes to the assignments the published conformance suite asserts: a header/body cross-check mismatch (`MCP-Protocol-Version` or `Mcp-Method` disagreeing with the request body) is now rejected with `-32020` (HeaderMismatch), and a request whose protocol-version header names a modern revision but whose body is missing the `_meta` envelope (or its required protocol-version key) is rejected with `-32602` invalid params naming the missing key(s). Both keep HTTP 400. These cells previously emitted a provisional `-32004` while the upstream error-code discussion was open. The envelope-less rejection on a modern-only endpoint (`-32022` with the supported-versions list), the 2025-era serving paths, and the client-side probe handling are unchanged.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:241:    **Tools:** Unknown or disabled tool calls now return JSON-RPC protocol errors with code `-32602` (InvalidParams) instead of `CallToolResult` with `isError: true`. Callers who checked `result.isError` for unknown tools should catch rejected promises instead.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:243:    **Resources:** Unknown resource reads now return error code `-32002` (ResourceNotFound) instead of `-32602` (InvalidParams).\n./packages/codemod/test/commentInsertion.test.ts:75:            `const code = ErrorCode.InvalidParams;`,\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:32:        const proto = new ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, 'bad');\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:45:        const proto = new ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, 'x');\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:77:        const foreignPlainProto = new protocolErrors.ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, 'x');\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:88:        const reconstructed = protocolErrors.ProtocolError.fromError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, 'gone', {\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2025-11-25.test.ts:92:    ReadResourceRequestParams: (sdk: SDKTypes.ReadResourceRequestParams, spec: SpecTypes.ReadResourceRequestParams) => {\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2025-11-25.test.ts:373:    ReadResourceRequest: (sdk: WithJSONRPCRequest<SDKTypes.ReadResourceRequest>, spec: SpecTypes.ReadResourceRequest) => {\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2025-11-25.test.ts:377:    ReadResourceResult: (sdk: SDKTyp