/src/server/mcp.ts:1388:    /** Cache hint applied to this template's `resources/read` results on the 2026-07-28 revision. */\n./packages/server/src/server/mcp.ts:1390:    readCallback: ReadResourceTemplateCallback;\n./packages/server/src/server/mcp.ts:1399:        callback?: ReadResourceTemplateCallback;\n./packages/server/src/server/mcp.ts:1465:                throw new ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, `Invalid arguments for prompt ${name}: ${parseResult.error}`);\n./packages/core-internal/test/types/errorSurfacePins.test.ts:46:            InvalidParams: -32602,\n./packages/core-internal/test/types/errorSurfacePins.test.ts:122:        const error = new ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, 'oops', { extra: 1 });\n./packages/core-internal/test/types/errorSurfacePins.test.ts:166:        // -32602 without `data.uri` is an ordinary Invalid Params, not resource-not-found.\n./packages/core-internal/test/types/errorSurfacePins.test.ts:173:        // A server's own Invalid Params with `data.uri` (e.g. a \"uri must be\n./packages/middleware/node/test/toNodeHandler.test.ts:46:    const name = b.method === 'resources/read' ? b.params.uri : b.params.name;\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/inputRequiredDriver.test.ts:240:            method: 'resources/read',\n./packages/server/src/server/serverEventBus.ts:125: * contains the event's URI exactly (per the spec: \"for these resource URIs\").\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/standardHeaderValidation.test.ts:9: * `prompts/get` / `resources/read` request, when the `Mcp-Name` header\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/standardHeaderValidation.test.ts:106:    test('a resources/read without an Mcp-Name header is rejected and names params.uri', () => {\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/standardHeaderValidation.test.ts:107:        const { request, route } = modernPost('resources/read', { uri: 'file:///a' }, { mcpMethod: 'resources/read' });\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/standardHeaderValidation.test.ts:165:    test('a matching Mcp-Name on a resources/read compares against params.uri', () => {\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/standardHeaderValidation.test.ts:167:        const { request, route } = modernPost('resources/read', { uri }, { mcpMethod: 'resources/read', mcpName: uri });\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/standardHeaderValidation.test.ts:172:        expect(MCP_NAME_HEADER_SOURCE).toEqual({ 'tools/call': 'name', 'prompts/get': 'name', 'resources/read': 'uri' });\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:60:type WReadResourceResult = z4.infer<typeof Wire2026.ReadResourceResultSchema>;\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:70:type WReadResourceRequest = z4.infer<typeof Wire2026.ReadResourceRequestSchema>;\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:75:type WResourceRequestParams = WReadResourceRequest['params'];\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:104:    | WReadResourceRequest\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:138:type WReadResourceRequestParamsRetry = WReadResourceRequest['params'];\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:141:type WReadResourceResultResponse = z4.infer<typeof Wire2026.ReadResourceResultResponseSchema>;\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:151:    | WReadResourceResult\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:226:    InvalidParamsError: (sdk: SDKTypes.InvalidParamsError, spec: SpecTypes.InvalidParamsError) => {\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:539:    ReadResourceResult: (sdk: WReadResourceResult, spec: SpecTypes.ReadResourceResult) => {\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:746:    ReadResourceRequestParams: (sdk: WReadResourceRequestParamsRetry, spec: SpecTypes.ReadResourceRequestParams) => {\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:750:    ReadResourceRequest: (sdk: WithJSONRPCRequest<WReadResourceRequest>, spec: SpecTypes.ReadResourceRequest) => {\n./packages/core-internal/test/spec.types.2026-07-28.test.ts:762:    ReadResourceResultResponse: (sdk: WReadResourceResultResponse, spec: SpecTypes.ReadResourceResultResponse) => {\n./packages/core-internal/test/corpus/specCorpus.test.ts:54:    'InvalidParamsError',\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/inboundClassification.test.ts:220:    test('a modern header on a claim-less body is rejected with invalid params naming the missing _meta envelope', () => {\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/inboundClassification.test.ts:331:        // Validated exactly like a request claim: invalid params naming the\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/protocol.test.ts:1124:            code: ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams,\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/inboundLadderCellSheet.test.ts:10: * disagreements, `-32602` invalid params naming the missing key(s) for a\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/inboundLadderCellSheet.test.ts:148:        rationale: 'A present claim with a malformed envelope is invalid params naming the key — never a silent legacy fallthrough.'\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/inboundLadderCellSheet.test.ts:190:            'A notification claim with a malformed protocol-version value is invalid params naming the key — exactly like the ' +\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/inboundLadderCellSheet.test.ts:263:            'envelope: invalid params naming the missing key(s), never an upgrade and never a silent legacy fallthrough.'\n./packages/core-internal/test/shared/inboundLadderCellSheet.test.ts:328:            'with invalid params; the mismatch is never reached.'\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:352: * {@includeCode ./examples/InvalidParamsError/unknown-tool.json}\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:355: * {@includeCode ./examples/InvalidParamsError/invalid-tool-arguments.json}\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:358: * {@includeCode ./examples/InvalidParamsError/unknown-prompt.json}\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:361: * {@includeCode ./examples/InvalidParamsError/invalid-cursor.json}\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:365:export interface InvalidParamsError extends Error {\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1169: * Parameters for a `resources/read` request.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1171: * @category `resources/read`\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1173:export interface ReadResourceRequestParams extends ResourceRequestParams, InputResponseRequestParams {}\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1176: * Sent from the client to the server, to read a specific resource URI.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1179: * {@includeCode ./examples/ReadResourceRequest/read-resource-request.json}\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1181: * @category `resources/read`\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1183:export interface ReadResourceRequest extends JSONRPCRequest {\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1184:    method: 'resources/read';\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1185:    params: ReadResourceRequestParams;\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1189: * The result returned by the server for a {@link ReadResourceRequest | resources/read} request.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1192: * {@includeCode ./examples/ReadResourceResult/file-resource-contents.json}\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1194: * @category `resources/read`\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1196:export interface ReadResourceResult extends CacheableResult {\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1201: * A successful response from the server for a {@link ReadResourceRequest | resources/read} request.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1204: * {@includeCode ./examples/ReadResourceResultResponse/read-resource-result-response.json}\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1207: * {@includeCode ./examples/ReadResourceResultResponse/read-resource-result-response-with-ttl.json}\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1209: * @category `resources/read`\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1211:export interface ReadResourceResultResponse extends JSONRPCResultResponse {\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1212:    result: ReadResourceResult | InputRequiredResult;\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1251:     * Subscribe to {@link ResourceUpdatedNotification | notifications/resources/updated} for these resource URIs.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:1431:     * A URI template (according to RFC 6570) that can be used to construct resource URIs.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:3089:    | ReadResourceRequest\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:3122:    | ReadResourceResult\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/specTypeSchema.ts:133:    'ReadResourceRequestSchema',\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/specTypeSchema.ts:134:    'ReadResourceRequestParamsSchema',\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/specTypeSchema.ts:135:    'ReadResourceResultSchema',\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:59: *   (invalid params) naming the missing key(s), on HTTP 400.\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:291:        codes: [ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams],\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:312:        codes: [ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams],\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:378: * `-32602` (invalid params) deliberately has NO entry: the only invalid-params\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:464:    'resources/read': 'uri'\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:480: *   `prompts/get`, or `resources/read` request whose body carries the\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:683:                    ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams,\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:712:    // is missing required params: it is rejected with invalid params naming the\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:726:                ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams,\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:764:                    ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams,\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/errors.ts:79:        // own Invalid Params that happens to carry `data.uri` alongside other\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/errors.ts:83:        if (code === ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams || code === ProtocolErrorCode.ResourceNotFound) {\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/errors.ts:110: * Error type for a `resources/read` miss: the requested resource does not\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/errors.ts:111: * exist. The wire code is `-32602` (Invalid Params) on every protocol\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/errors.ts:118: * any other `-32602` is an ordinary Invalid Params). For backwards compatibility, clients should also\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/errors.ts:131:        super(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, message, { uri });\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inputRequired.ts:6: * `prompts/get`, `resources/read`) requests additional client input by\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/authUtils.ts:2: * Utilities for handling OAuth resource URIs.\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/authUtils.ts:8: * states that resource URIs \"MUST NOT include a fragment component\".\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:45:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - `resources/read` for an unknown URI now answers with JSON-RPC error code `-32602`\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:46:  (Invalid Params) on every protocol revision, with `error.data.uri` echoing the\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:70:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Results of the cacheable 2026-07-28 operations (`tools/list`, `prompts/list`, `resources/list`, `resources/templates/list`, `resources/read`, `server/discover`) now always carry the revision's required `ttlMs`/`cacheScope` fields when served on that revision, defaulting to `ttlMs: 0` / `cacheScope: 'private'`. Servers can configure the emitted values with the new `ServerOptions.cacheHints` option (per operation) and the new `cacheHint` member of the `registerResource` config (per resource); resolution is per field, most specific author first: cache fields returned by a handler win over the per-resource hint, which wins over the per-operation hint, and configured hints are validated at construction/registration time (`RangeError` on invalid values). Responses on 2025-era connections are unchanged and never carry these fields. Note for untyped callers: `registerResource` now interprets a `cacheHint` key in its config object — it is validated and kept out of the resource's list metadata, where it was previously passed through as ordinary metadata.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:87:- [#2381](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2381) [`f0bf785`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/f0bf785239af67f0cfce24575fec9c1193deaff1) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Serve `input_required` handlers on 2025-era connections: the legacy shim (on by default) converts each embedded request of an `input_required` return into a real server→client request (`elicitation/create`, `sampling/createMessage`, `roots/list`) over the live session — stamped with the originating request's id for stream association — and re-enters the handler with the collected `inputResponses` until a final result. Handlers are written once in the 2026 `inputRequired(...)` style and serve both eras; the previous loud `-32603` failure remains available via `ServerOptions.inputRequired.legacyShim: false`. Knobs: `inputRequired.maxRounds` (default 8) and `inputRequired.roundTimeoutMs` (default 600 000 ms per leg; legs carry a progressToken so a client reporting progress mid-leg resets the leg timeout). Semantics mirror the modern client driver exactly: per-round replaced `inputResponses`, byte-exact `requestState` echo with the verify hook running every round, paced requestState-only rounds, and elicitation accepted content passed through UNVALIDATED (the handler validates via the schema-aware `acceptedContent` overload, exactly as on the 2026 era). URL-mode legs synthesize the `elicitationId` the 2025-11-25 wire requires. Failures surface per family (`tools/call` → `isError` tool result; `prompts/get` / `resources/read` → JSON-RPC error); stateless legacy HTTP degrades to a clean capability refusal; the shim emits no progress of its own (the originating progressToken is the handler's single must-increase stream — the shim never adds a second author to it).\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:95:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Add the server side of multi round-trip requests (protocol revision 2026-07-28, SEP-2322). Handlers for `tools/call`, `prompts/get`, and `resources/read` can return the value built by `inputRequired()` (exported from the server package together with `acceptedContent()`)\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:101:  wire behavior is unchanged. An optional `ServerOptions.requestState.verify` hook lets a server integrity-check the echoed `requestState` before the handler runs — a throw answers the wire-level `-32602` Invalid Params error with `data.reason: 'invalid_request_state'`; the SDK provides no default verification.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:110:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - SEP-2243 standard-header server-side validation (protocol revision 2026-07-28). On the modern (2026-07-28) serving path, `createMcpHandler` now enforces the required `Mcp-Method` and `Mcp-Name` standard request headers in addition to the existing `MCP-Protocol-Version` and `Mcp-Method` cross-checks: a modern request without an `Mcp-Method` header, a `tools/call` / `prompts/get` / `resources/read` request without an `Mcp-Name` header, an `Mcp-Name` header carrying an invalid `=?base64?…?=` sentinel, and an `Mcp-Name` header whose (decoded) value disagrees with the body's `params.name` / `params.uri` are all rejected with `400 Bad Request` and JSON-RPC `-32020` (`HeaderMismatch`). The 2025-era serving paths are unchanged.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:154:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Pin the modern (2026-07-28) HTTP serving path's rejection codes to the assignments the published conformance suite asserts: a header/body cross-check mismatch (`MCP-Protocol-Version` or `Mcp-Method` disagreeing with the request body) is now rejected with `-32020` (HeaderMismatch), and a request whose protocol-version header names a modern revision but whose body is missing the `_meta` envelope (or its required protocol-version key) is rejected with `-32602` invalid params naming the missing key(s). Both keep HTTP 400. These cells previously emitted a provisional `-32004` while the upstream error-code discussion was open. The envelope-less rejection on a modern-only endpoint (`-32022` with the supported-versions list), the 2025-era serving paths, and the client-side probe handling are unchanged.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:296:    **Tools:** Unknown or disabled tool calls now return JSON-RPC protocol errors with code `-32602` (InvalidParams) instead of `CallToolResult` with `isError: true`. Callers who checked `result.isError` for unknown tools should catch rejected promises instead.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:298:    **Resources:** Unknown resource reads now return error code `-32002` (ResourceNotFound) instead of `-32602` (InvalidParams).\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:706: * Parameters for a `resources/read` request.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:708: * @category `resources/read`\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:711:export interface ReadResourceRequestParams extends ResourceRequestParams {}\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:714: * Sent from the client to the server, to read a specific resource URI.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:716: * @category `resources/read`\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:718:export interface ReadResourceRequest extends JSONRPCRequest {\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:719:    method: 'resources/read';\n.